A FALSE RESULT I CAUGHT IN MY OWN HARNESS, recorded because it is the kind that gets published. The first
pass over these runs reported ONE verdict changed, which is precisely what this change promised could not
happen. The cause was my re-decide script calling the verdict without red_fixture and red_expect, so a RED-OK
fixture graded as a plain FAIL. Supplying the two arguments the run actually had gives 22 of 22 unchanged. I
checked which of the two it was rather than explaining the one away.

A SECOND ONE, in the same session and the same shape. I first reported the split as 13 irq_entry; it is 15.
My counting regex required the name at the END of the reason string and silently dropped the two red-fixture
reasons that carry text after it. The totals were right and only the split was wrong.

